{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on 4cb90391: adopt the narrow Continue branch for the proven plan-only state, with the conditions you stated and two more.\n\nAdopted as stated: same plan, operation, home, actor and inputs; zero receiver issuance pointers, no handoff, no STARTED, no config, no keys or enrollment originals, no owner invitation pointer; Continue creates only the first maintained issuance root in new mode, with its private original durable before any act; any surviving pointer, orphan or conflict still stops; Check stays read-only; no retained signature, key, secret, deadline or native room is remade. Focused custody tests against the actual engine and a new source gate accompany the repair before exact-head review.\n\nTwo further conditions. First, the branch proves the plan is the same plan: it compares the retained identity plan's digest with the plan it is about to continue, and stops on any difference. Second, the repair closes the diagnosis gap: scratch-all-2 closed in 2.05 seconds before the root was retained and the pre-root error is unknown. The helper retains the pre-root exit status and stderr of such a start in the safe metadata directory before it exits, so a recurrence is diagnosable from the public receipt. Report the recurrence cause when you find it; if it is a product defect rather than a helper defect, it goes on the S1 head.\n\nNothing in this ruling changes the S1 scope, the approved scratch and real rooms, or the rule that a missing pre-envelope original stops. dap-demo stays on its current deployment and register while the run settles.","body":{"no_git_artifact":"true","stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:4cb903918872f1679bc0ece85a6089b75f02cb73 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:070231aadcb17348891458bc2eedb5bbf529860c","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}